Kennita asked whether anyone has had any personal experience with light and
sound machines that alter brainwaves.  I have a "Voyager Galaxy XL" mind
machine. The lights in the goggles flash on and off at certain frequencies
that correspond to brainwave frequencies associated with different states
of consciousness.  The goal is to trick the brain into entering the desired
state of consciousness.

It's hard to say how effective it has been at reducing the number of
hours of sleep, but I use it most nights to get to sleep very quickly.
I have noticed an increase of vivid dreams, sometimes shortly after
using the mind machine (when taking a nap in the afternoon, for
instance).  

I have more information on them if you want it, including scientific
studies on the effects of light and sound technology. (By the way,
when I bought mine I also purchased a distributor's license, so if
anybody's REALLY interested...:))

I think I'll go put mine on right now. Good night everybody.


