Fundamental, basic, deserving of a special term ("Axiom").  Also, there's 
something fishy about an argument that goes "This is true because anyone who
gets into an argument about it with me is going to lose."  It's like saying,
"Look at this Maginot Line I've built.  *Nobody's* going to get through *this*
one, boy."  Predicting the outcome seems a poor way of preparing for truly
worthy criticism, much less staying open to it, although it's good to have
a sense of where one stands.

