To me it seems more apt to say that in one sense I can't know.  I can't know,
and know I know, and know I know I know...forever.  As a matter of
philosophical cleanness, that's the ultimate state of things, worth keeping
in mind back there somewhere.  But given that it's true all of the time, it's 
not usually worth mentioning.

> If Bartley justified PCR on utilitarian
