Hmm.  There are innate processes that generate processes, some of which are
winnowed, but some of which generate further processes...that eventually
generate ideas.  Just as not all reflexes are ideas, not all idea-generating
processes are theories of knowledge or need to be.  So when *do* you need 
an actual theory of knowledge, actual ideas about it?

